<h2>Course Overview and Goals</h2>
<p>This material organizes the <strong>"Claude Code Basics / Minho Hwang"</strong> hands-on course in the order of the video. For non-developers the terminal is an unfamiliar place, but once you clear <strong>the one hurdle &mdash; "create a folder and run <code>claude</code> from that location"</strong> &mdash; the AI takes care of most of the work from there. Today's goal is to get comfortable with the terminal.</p>

<h3>What this course will let you do</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Create a folder in the terminal and run Claude Code.</li>
    <li>Give your own working instructions with <code>CLAUDE.md</code>.</li>
    <li>Ask for web research &rarr; file saving &rarr; website generation in one go.</li>
    <li>Turn repetitive work into a <strong>Skill</strong> and specialized work into an <strong>Agent</strong> for reuse.</li>
    <li>Install plugins to handle PDF, PPT, and Excel documents.</li>
    <li>Manage usage, context, and sessions to control quality and cost.</li>
</ul>

