<p>Once you are past the basic hurdle, the <strong>Harness</strong> is waiting next. With a harness, a few lines of prompt can produce an entire book of more than 200&ndash;300 pages. The example shown in the course works like this.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Create <strong>several agents</strong> (say, five) to write the book.</li>
    <li>A research agent prepares the book's sources.</li>
    <li>The agents <strong>write in parallel</strong> and report when they're done.</li>
    <li>It even generates the illustrations needed and inserts them at exactly the right places.</li>
    <li>It converts the result into Markdown and PDF, and builds a page-turning website too. &mdash; <strong>about an hour in total</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>In other words, you can build "my own book for people starting out with Claude Code" yourself. The harness itself is covered in a separate later session.</p>

